<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Value after depreciation</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>[[if test="is(ix=1)"]]A boda boda rider buys a motorbike[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=2)"]]A school buys a laptop[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=3)"]]A transport company in Nakuru buys a lorry[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=4)"]]A matatu owner buys a matatu[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=5)"]]A miller buys a posho mill[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=6)"]]A shop buys a delivery van[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=7)"]]A school buys a photocopier[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=8)"]]A farm buys a solar water pump[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=9)"]]A driver in Mombasa buys a tuk-tuk[[/if]][[if test="is(ix=10)"]]A tailoring workshop buys an embroidery machine[[/if]] for Ksh \({@ksh(P)@}\). It depreciates at \({@r@}\%\) a year (reducing balance).</p><p>(a) Find its value after \({@n@}\) years, to the nearest shilling.</p><p>Ksh [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p><p>(b) Find the total depreciation.</p><p>Ksh [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Each year's loss is a percentage of what the item is worth at the start of that year, so the losses get smaller. Each year the value is multiplied by \(1 - \frac{ {@r@} }{100} = {@dd(mult)@}\).</p><p>(a) \(V = {@ksh(P)@} \times {@dd(mult)@}^{ {@n@} } = {@ksh(V)@}\), so the value is Ksh \({@ksh(floor(V+1/2))@}\) to the nearest shilling.</p><p>(b) Depreciation \(= P - V = {@ksh(P)@} - {@ksh(V)@} = {@ksh(Dp)@}\)[[if test="not(integerp(Dp))"]], about Ksh \({@ksh(floor(Dp+1/2))@}\)[[/if]].</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[kgrp(n) := block([s, out, k], s: string(n), k: slength(s), if k < 5 then s else (out: "", while k > 3 do (out: sconcat("\\,", substring(s, k-2, k+1), out), k: k-3), sconcat(substring(s, 1, k+1), out)));
ksh(v) := block([c, w, f], c: floor(100*v+1/2), w: floor(c/100), f: c-100*w, if f = 0 then kgrp(w) else sconcat(kgrp(w), ".", if f < 10 then "0" else "", string(f)));
dd(v) := if integerp(v) then v else if integerp(10*v) then dispdp(float(v),1) else if integerp(100*v) then dispdp(float(v),2) else if integerp(1000*v) then dispdp(float(v),3) else dispdp(float(v),4);
ix: 1+rand(10);
/* Design: value falling by a percentage each year. [P, r, n]. Source: adapted from SMP GCSE Higher book 1, chapter 8, C10 and T2(b). */
L: [[185000,17,3],[72000,25,2],[2600000,13,4],[5400000,16,3],[340000,10,5],[1450000,21,3],[58000,35,2],[230000,16,4],[760000,22,3],[410000,14,5]];
E: L[ix];
P: E[1]; r: E[2]; n: E[3];
mult: 1-r/100;
V: P*mult^n;
Dp: P-V;
/* diagnostics */
Vl: P*(1-r*n/100);
Va: P*(1+r/100)^n;
Vm: P*mult^(n-1);
Dl: P*r*n/100;
D1: P*r/100;
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
