  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Commercial Arithmetic III: value after depreciation</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Essential 2.4 (c): Find the value of a machine or vehicle after several years of reducing-balance depreciation, and the total depreciation.</p><p id="edition">Essential</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Chapter 8 (Percentages), Section C, question C10, and Test yourself T2(b) of Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP GCSE Mathematics: Higher 1 for AQA, Edexcel and OCR two-tier GCSE mathematics, Cambridge University Press, 2006: a value falling by the same percentage each year; new items and numbers.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Essential Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
